    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I’ve not directly used AI for math learning, but during university research, tools like Wolfram Alpha helped verify complex proofs. My experience suggested they’re most useful for cross-disciplinary validation—not teaching fundamentals. The low neuroticism and high conscientiousness likely meant I trusted algorithms less than someone else might.",
